IN=[('National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal','https://cybercrime.gov.in/','The Government of India portal for reporting cybercrime, including hacked accounts and online fraud. The national helpline is 1930.'),('Grievance Appellate Committee','https://gac.gov.in/','Under the IT Rules 2021, you can appeal here if a platform’s Grievance Officer does not resolve your complaint.')]
INOTE='<h2 id="india-notes">Notes for India</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar, PAN, passport, voter ID or driving licence can work as ID when the name matches the profile. Upload a clear photo; mask the Aadhaar number if Meta’s screen allows it.</li><li>Under the IT Rules 2021, large platforms have a Grievance Officer for India. If a grievance is not resolved, the Grievance Appellate Committee at gac.gov.in takes appeals.</li><li>For hacking or money lost to fraud, report at cybercrime.gov.in or call 1930.</li><li>Turn off any VPN before you appeal, and use your usual SIM and phone.</li></ul>'
